land and that's hugely exciting  for the future of this franchise if  reeves continues at the helm and that's  where my excitement comes from here for  the future the future of this franchise  has me incredibly excited off the back  of this wonderful film there are a huge  number of hints towards future content  throughout and i can't wait to see how  they play out i've not even mentioned  colin farrell's penguin despite the fact  that it's one of the most stand out  performances in this film and some of  the best transformative acting in recent  memory the fact he's getting his own hbo  spin-off series that focuses harder on  the corrupt aspects of gotham's police  system is so exciting then of course  there's also the part where batman  injects himself with this green fluid  was it just adrenaline was it venom  hinting at bane or the addiction story  from the comics of the same name heck  there's even what appears to be a joker  cameo at one point this film is just  packed full of detail i cannot emphasize  enough just how much i adore it i do  genuinely think this may very well be my  favorite batman film to date now that  may be recency bias talking but the way  it brings the source material to the big  screen is just so uncompromising and  perfectly accurate and with such a  compelling story and awesome  performances to boot i can just barely  fault it if i had to put a score in it i  would probably go with a 9 out of 10 a  strong 9 out of 10. i think also because  of this it means retroactively it  affects some of the scores that came  before most critically sending halle  berry's catwoman into the negatives  justice in conclusion it is my firm  belief that all-time comic fans will  love this incredible three-hour  spectacular that doesn't feel at all  like three hours as always subscribe for  more reviews like this and i'll see you  all next time thanks for watching  [Music]  you
 

